WEBVTT

00:10:59.911 --> 00:11:02.811
that I was a lot more interested
in the origins of the plants

00:11:02.835 --> 00:11:04.382
than in the plants themselves --

00:11:04.406 --> 00:11:07.125
the history and ethnobiography
of these plants.

00:11:07.149 --> 00:11:08.961
When did these tulips come to America?

00:11:08.985 --> 00:11:13.095
Why wisteria? Who was
the missionary who found this?

00:11:13.119 --> 00:11:15.485
What is a native plant?
What is an imported plant?

00:11:15.509 --> 00:11:17.656
What is the intersection of history

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:21.662
between humans and these
things that we grow and why?

00:11:21.686 --> 00:11:23.861
And once I started looking into that,

00:11:23.885 --> 00:11:28.272
I got really interested, suddenly,
in 19th-century botanical exploration.

00:11:28.296 --> 00:11:31.926
And once I got interested in that,
I got interested in the study of evolution